Style contract: .kiro/steering/devsecops-image-style.md
Save the result as this file's name without ".todo": pipeline-end-to-end-v1.png
----------------------------------------------------------------------
A clean, modern technical infographic for an enterprise DevSecOps course.
Institutional, precise, calm, authoritative mood — security shown as good
engineering, never as threat.

IMPORTANT: do NOT render any title, heading, sub-heading, or course name inside
the image. Draw ONLY the short labels listed below. No sentences anywhere.
Do NOT draw fire, flames, embers, hooded hackers, or skulls.

SUBJECT: the full end-to-end DevSecOps pipeline — six security gates in sequence
from commit to a policy-admitted deploy.

ELEMENTS: a source-code "{ }" chip enters at the far left and flows left to right
through six sequential numbered gate nodes, each a rounded box with one simple
tool icon and a small pass/fail gate symbol. After the sixth gate, a verified
container with a padlock-and-check badge exits into a "prod" namespace cloud on
the right. One dropped red branch off a gate shows that any failing gate stops
the flow. Clean single horizontal flow.

LABELS (the ONLY text in the image — short, exact): commit, 1 Gitleaks,
2 Semgrep, 3 Trivy CVE, 4 Trivy SBOM, 5 cosign, 6 Kyverno, prod.

Visual language: flat-vector meets soft 3D, clean geometric shapes, rounded
corners, subtle depth and soft shadows. Security motifs are shields, check
badges, gates, and padlock-with-checkmark icons.

Color palette: soft light background (white or very light blue-grey); deep NAVY
and TEAL as the base; CYAN highlights; EMERALD-GREEN success accents. Use RED
only for the single "failing gate stops the flow" branch — a flat color, never an
alarm wash.

Composition: one clear subject, generous negative space, balanced, crisp edges,
no grain. 16:9 landscape.

Strictly avoid: ANY title or heading text in the image; fire, flames, embers,
glowing heat; cartoonish or mascot elements; neon colors; organic textures;
hand-drawn or sketchy feel; hand-made or decorative typography; watermarks;
agency seals; rank insignia; decorative borders; readable paragraphs or gibberish
text; skulls; hooded hackers; matrix rain; glitch; warning-triangle spam.

High detail, professional, enterprise-grade. Aspect ratio 16:9.
